WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.542 --> 00:00:03.542
&lt;i&gt;Stranger Things &lt;/i&gt;returns
in 2022

00:00:03.625 --> 00:00:06.292
and, thanks to a series of
cryptic location teasers,

00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:09.750
we're as hungry for answers
as Eleven is for Eggos.

00:00:12.417 --> 00:00:13.750
What better way to
fill the time

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:15.083
before season four arrives

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.542
than to go and round up some
of the wildest fan theories

00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:20.125
about where &lt;i&gt;Stranger Things&lt;/i&gt;
could go?

00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:22.625
To be clear,
we're confirming nothing.

00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:25.042
These are just fan theories.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.208
So let's jump in.

00:00:28.042 --> 00:00:30.417
Our big question at
the end of season three was:

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.625
Is Hopper really dead?

00:00:32.708 --> 00:00:34.833
In the emotional finale,
we saw Joyce Byers

00:00:34.917 --> 00:00:36.833
destroying the gates
to the Upside Down,

00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:38.708
evaporating every Russian
in the room

00:00:38.792 --> 00:00:40.542
and we're led to believe

00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:41.792
Hopper along with them.

00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.708
We ended the season mourning
our beloved police chief

00:00:44.792 --> 00:00:46.000
only for the action
to cut to

00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:47.917
a Russian outpost
in Kamchatka

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.208
where two guards decide
not to feed

00:00:50.292 --> 00:00:52.250
the American to
their Demogorgon.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.792
Fans suspected
this might refer to Hopper,

00:00:56.875 --> 00:00:58.417
and that seems to be
confirmed by

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.958
the Russian location teaser
showing

00:01:00.042 --> 00:01:01.500
a shaved David Harbour

00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:03.458
working in
a snowy prison camp.

00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:06.083
So this confirms that Hopper
is alive and well, right?

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:08.000
Some fans think
it might be a fake out

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:10.583
or, at least,
not as simple as it seems.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.625
One theory is that,
while Hopper is alive,

00:01:12.708 --> 00:01:16.417
he's actually trapped
in the past in 1959:

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.500
a year that's very important
to season four,

00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:19.917
as we'll discuss later.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.125
The main thinking behind
this take

00:01:21.208 --> 00:01:24.208
is that the Russians in
Kamchatka have a Demogorgon.

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:25.167
The logic goes that

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.667
if there is only one of
these monsters

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.417
and that one was destroyed
at the end of season one,

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.208
then this scene
would have to be in the past

00:01:31.292 --> 00:01:32.542
to make sense.

00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:36.042
It would also gel with
the nod to

00:01:36.125 --> 00:01:38.125
&lt;i&gt;Back to the Future&lt;/i&gt;
in season three.

00:01:38.208 --> 00:01:40.250
That's another story
about people from the 1980s

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.500
getting thrown back
to the 1950s.

00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:45.167
It's not the only time
travel theory in this video,

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.125
so do hold on to
that thought.

00:01:53.042 --> 00:01:55.833
Another theory is that
Hopper is alive in Russia

00:01:55.917 --> 00:01:56.917
in 1986,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.958
but the American
the guards refer to is

00:01:59.042 --> 00:02:02.125
actually Martin Brenner,
the ice cold director of

00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:05.125
Hawkins National Laboratory
last seen getting munched on

00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:06.542
at the end of season one.

00:02:08.042 --> 00:02:10.042
It would make sense that
Russians obsessed with

00:02:10.125 --> 00:02:12.208
accessing the Upside Down
would maybe work with

00:02:12.292 --> 00:02:15.250
the scientist who discovered
the gate in the first place.

00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:16.500
The theory also argues that,

00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:18.250
if Hopper is
the special prisoner

00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:19.583
mentioned
at the end of season three,

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.750
why is he left doing hard
labour on a railway line

00:02:22.833 --> 00:02:24.500
in the Russian
location teaser?

00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:26.875
I don't know!
I've never done this before!

00:02:28.792 --> 00:02:30.083
The Brenner idea ties into

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.750
another batch of
fan theories

00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:33.958
that Brenner definitely has
a role to play

00:02:34.042 --> 00:02:35.500
in season four.

00:02:35.583 --> 00:02:36.917
The lab teaser
for season four

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.667
takes us back to
the Rainbow Room,

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.583
where young Eleven
and the other test subjects

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:42.000
at
Hawkins National Laboratory

00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:43.625
were experimented on

00:02:43.708 --> 00:02:45.833
by Mathew Modine's
creepy researcher.

00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:47.583
This scene could just be
a flashback

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.417
to Eleven's
original captivity,

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.375
but some fans wonder
if it might be proof

00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:54.000
that Brenner survived
his Demogorgon encounter

00:02:54.083 --> 00:02:55.833
and is setting up
a second lab

00:02:55.917 --> 00:02:58.250
to raise a fresh batch
of psychic warriors.

00:02:58.333 --> 00:03:01.292
The fact that one of the
episode titles is "Papa",

00:03:01.375 --> 00:03:02.792
the name Eleven called
Brenner in the past,

00:03:02.875 --> 00:03:05.417
certainly backs
that idea up.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.375
Yes, Papa.

00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:09.208
Other fans point to
the clock in the teaser

00:03:09.292 --> 00:03:11.042
and throughout all the
season four teasers

00:03:11.125 --> 00:03:13.083
as being another hint of
time travel,

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:14.958
that instead of this being
a flashback,

00:03:15.042 --> 00:03:17.333
Eleven somehow ends up
travelling back to

00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:20.000
the Rainbow Room
to meet her former nemesis.

00:03:20.083 --> 00:03:22.583
Another really wild idea
suggests that

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:23.833
Brenner will return,

00:03:23.917 --> 00:03:27.500
but that he'll be
the Mind Flayer in disguise.

00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:28.417
I mean, hey,

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.583
look at the damage it did
by possessing Billy,

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.417
a simple
swimming pool attendant!

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.792
A body with Brenner's
access would be

00:03:34.875 --> 00:03:36.500
a juicier target.

00:03:37.792 --> 00:03:39.250
Go to hell,
you piece of shit!

00:03:42.458 --> 00:03:44.583
Oh! And another
Rainbow Room side note.

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:45.792
One theory believes that

00:03:45.875 --> 00:03:47.583
season four will introduce
more of

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:50.042
Eleven's fellow
child test subjects.

00:03:50.125 --> 00:03:52.000
We've already met
Eight, aka Kali,

00:03:52.083 --> 00:03:52.958
in season two

00:03:53.042 --> 00:03:55.167
and had a taste of
her distinct powers.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:59.250
I can make people see, or
not see, whatever I choose.

00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:01.333
And the supporting
&lt;i&gt;Stranger Things &lt;/i&gt;comic books

00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:04.875
feature other numbered
children, like Six and Nine.

00:04:04.958 --> 00:04:06.542
With the lab teaser showing
multiple children,

00:04:06.625 --> 00:04:09.583
could we finally see
Eleven go full X-Men

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:11.417
with
her fellow test subjects?

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.417
Time will tell.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:13.458
Yoohoo!

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.500
One thing's obvious from
the location teasers,

00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:21.000
and that is that &lt;i&gt;Stranger&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Things &lt;/i&gt;is hitting the road

00:04:21.083 --> 00:04:22.042
in season four

00:04:22.125 --> 00:04:24.000
with the California
and Russia snapshots

00:04:24.083 --> 00:04:25.375
hinting at a global scale.

00:04:25.458 --> 00:04:27.750
Fan theories are trying to
make sense of it all,

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:30.083
working out how characters
in different locations

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:31.167
could interact.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.417
One theory wonders
if Joyce will go hunting

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.583
for Hopper in Russia

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:36.833
after receiving
a Russian doll in the post,

00:04:36.917 --> 00:04:38.417
suggesting that
she could team up with

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.542
conspiracist Murray
on the Soviet trip.

00:04:40.625 --> 00:04:42.083
That may also explain

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:43.833
the mysterious Russian dolls

00:04:43.917 --> 00:04:46.625
some fans of the show
received in the post.

00:04:46.708 --> 00:04:48.708
Even trickier is linking
the lab teaser

00:04:48.792 --> 00:04:49.875
to the other events.

00:04:49.958 --> 00:04:51.750
One viewer suggests
a link exists

00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:53.625
between Hopper and Brenner's
old lab

00:04:53.708 --> 00:04:55.333
that maybe
his daughter Sarah

00:04:55.417 --> 00:04:57.583
once had something to do
with the Rainbow Room.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.375
There's a very old
fan theory that

00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:01.167
this scene of Hopper crying
over his daughter

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.125
in season one

00:05:02.208 --> 00:05:05.375
is actually set inside
Hawkins Lab, for example.

00:05:05.458 --> 00:05:07.917
Another fan spotted that
the tag line for the season

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.583
"We're not
in Hawkins anymore"

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:11.542
has connections to
the Wizard of Oz's

00:05:11.625 --> 00:05:13.375
"We're not
in Kansas anymore",

00:05:13.458 --> 00:05:16.417
where Dorothy famously went
over the rainbow.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.750
Rainbow. Rainbow Room.

00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:20.625
Does this imply
the test chamber scene

00:05:20.708 --> 00:05:22.958
in the lab tease
isn't in Hawkins?

00:05:23.042 --> 00:05:26.167
Might that tie it to
Russia or California?

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.000
We're truly down
the rabbit hole now.

00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:30.000
No! Wait, that's
a different kids' story.

00:05:30.083 --> 00:05:32.500
And, as for the spooky
mansion in the Creel teaser,

00:05:32.583 --> 00:05:35.708
one eagle-eyed,
no, -eared viewer

00:05:35.792 --> 00:05:37.333
reminds us the ticking
of a clock was heard

00:05:37.417 --> 00:05:40.375
when El ventured into the
Upside Down in season one,

00:05:42.292 --> 00:05:43.875
which this theorist thinks

00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:45.792
ties the events
in the Creel House

00:05:45.875 --> 00:05:47.917
to anywhere
the Upside Down reaches.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.042
More clock theories
in a second.

00:05:52.458 --> 00:05:53.583
Let's stick with El
for a moment.

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:56.042
The California teaser shows
her yearning for home

00:05:56.125 --> 00:05:58.083
by building a cute model
of Hopper's cabin,

00:05:58.167 --> 00:05:59.542
but she might have
bigger problems

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.083
than feeling homesick.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:03.250
One question fans
definitely want answered

00:06:03.333 --> 00:06:05.958
in season four is whether
El will get her powers back.

00:06:06.042 --> 00:06:07.042
At the end of season three,

00:06:07.125 --> 00:06:08.083
her tie with
the supernatural

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.250
was seemingly severed
after fighting

00:06:10.333 --> 00:06:11.958
the physical form
of the Mind Flayer.

00:06:12.042 --> 00:06:13.667
Although there is
one fun theory that

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:14.750
perhaps it was Hopper

00:06:14.833 --> 00:06:16.125
who suppressed her powers
deliberately

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:17.042
to dissuade her from

00:06:17.125 --> 00:06:19.500
entering the dangerous
Russian base under the mall

00:06:19.583 --> 00:06:21.375
and to prevent her from
using her powers

00:06:21.458 --> 00:06:22.375
to track him to Russia.

00:06:22.958 --> 00:06:24.750
Quite why he'd do this
is fuzzy

00:06:24.833 --> 00:06:26.000
and the idea that
he put something

00:06:26.083 --> 00:06:28.208
in El's fizzy drink
to stop her powers

00:06:28.292 --> 00:06:29.583
is the kind of
mad conspiracy

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:31.750
you'd expect
from Murray Bauman.

00:06:31.833 --> 00:06:34.417
You do not get to
question me.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.625
However she lost them,

00:06:35.708 --> 00:06:38.708
fans agree that El's
abilities will reawaken

00:06:38.792 --> 00:06:39.708
in season four.

00:06:39.792 --> 00:06:42.250
Theorists think the shots
of El freaking out

00:06:42.333 --> 00:06:45.167
in the Rink-O-Mania have
big Carrie energy.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.375
We also see her being
picked on by smug students

00:06:47.458 --> 00:06:48.917
in her new
Californian school,

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.667
so she's likely
ready to snap.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.208
Could a lack
of roller skating prowess

00:06:53.292 --> 00:06:55.292
unclog
her super power blockage?

00:06:55.375 --> 00:06:56.500
Bully Eleven

00:06:56.583 --> 00:06:59.417
and the only thing you're
skating on is thin ice.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.917
-My arm!
-Go.

00:07:02.833 --> 00:07:05.167
Or could it be
a more emotional betrayal

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.500
that kickstarts
her cerebral capabilities?

00:07:07.583 --> 00:07:09.833
With El leaving Hawkins
at the end of season three

00:07:09.917 --> 00:07:12.458
to travel with the Byers to
their new Californian home,

00:07:12.542 --> 00:07:13.708
a few worried fans wonder if

00:07:13.792 --> 00:07:15.292
her long-distance
relationship

00:07:15.375 --> 00:07:17.083
with Mike won't work.

00:07:17.167 --> 00:07:18.708
Yes, it feels like
we're jinxing them

00:07:18.792 --> 00:07:20.292
just by entertaining
the thought,

00:07:20.375 --> 00:07:23.792
but some viewers think Mike
might find a new girlfriend.

00:07:23.875 --> 00:07:26.500
We know things got rocky
in places in season three

00:07:26.583 --> 00:07:28.917
and El's new bestie, Max,
encouraged her to be

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.958
more independent
in matters of love,

00:07:32.042 --> 00:07:34.250
but we're not sure we could
handle any more heartbreak,

00:07:34.333 --> 00:07:36.542
so we're going to pretend
we haven't heard that one.

00:07:36.625 --> 00:07:37.542
I love you, too.

00:07:39.875 --> 00:07:41.958
Another intriguing thread
to season four is

00:07:42.042 --> 00:07:43.958
the importance
of the Creel family

00:07:44.042 --> 00:07:46.458
introduced in the
Creel teaser for the show.

00:07:46.542 --> 00:07:47.625
According
to newspaper images

00:07:47.708 --> 00:07:48.917
released on social media,

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.875
the family were involved
in a terrible crime in 1959,

00:07:51.958 --> 00:07:53.917
explaining why some believe

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.458
Hopper may have travelled to
that year in particular.

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:58.875
What we do know is that,
27 years later,

00:07:58.958 --> 00:08:01.000
we see our Hawkins regulars
breaking in to

00:08:01.083 --> 00:08:03.542
the Creels' now abandoned
home, but, from here,

00:08:03.625 --> 00:08:05.792
the fan theories break
in multiple directions.

00:08:05.875 --> 00:08:07.292
One attentive fan thinks

00:08:07.375 --> 00:08:08.667
there's physical
similarities between

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.375
Mrs. Creel
and Karen, Wheeler,

00:08:10.458 --> 00:08:11.875
maybe suggesting
a family tie

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:13.667
that the gang
might investigate.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:16.583
Others hypothesise that the
casting of Robert Englund

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:17.667
as Victor Creel,

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.292
aka Freddy Krueger from
&lt;i&gt;A Nightmare on Elm Street,&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:23.125
might be a nod to
Nancy Wheeler's importance,

00:08:23.208 --> 00:08:25.083
as some fans note
the similarities between her

00:08:25.167 --> 00:08:28.292
and Nancy Thompson,
the heroine in &lt;i&gt;Elm Street&lt;/i&gt;.

00:08:28.375 --> 00:08:30.208
It would be meta as hell,

00:08:30.292 --> 00:08:32.833
but &lt;i&gt;Stranger Things &lt;/i&gt;doesn't
shy away from references.

00:08:32.917 --> 00:08:35.583
A more common theory is that
the creepy grandfather clock

00:08:35.667 --> 00:08:37.458
featured prominently
in the teaser is

00:08:37.542 --> 00:08:39.625
a gateway to
the Upside Down,

00:08:39.708 --> 00:08:41.375
much like the one
Nancy discovered in the tree

00:08:41.458 --> 00:08:42.458
in season one.

00:08:42.542 --> 00:08:44.958
Did a connection with
the twisted mirror dimension

00:08:45.042 --> 00:08:47.708
exist before Eleven opened
a gate in 1983

00:08:47.792 --> 00:08:51.083
and did it cast some
dark magic on the Creels?

00:08:51.167 --> 00:08:53.083
Or maybe the clock is just
another hint towards

00:08:53.167 --> 00:08:54.250
the time travel shenanigans

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.208
that pop up in loads of
these theories.

00:08:56.292 --> 00:08:59.750
Personally, we don't mind
the outcome as long as

00:08:59.833 --> 00:09:02.625
we get more Sherlock Holmes
quotes from Dustin.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:05.167
The world is full of
obvious things

00:09:06.667 --> 00:09:09.875
which nobody by any chance
ever observes.

00:09:09.958 --> 00:09:12.625
Of course, these are just
a sliver of the theories

00:09:12.708 --> 00:09:14.792
surrounding season four
of &lt;i&gt;Stranger Things&lt;/i&gt;.

00:09:14.875 --> 00:09:17.500
We've read hundreds of
out-there ideas

00:09:17.583 --> 00:09:19.167
from the fans,
from the idea that

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:21.083
the Upside Down is
a potential future Earth

00:09:21.167 --> 00:09:22.583
that Eleven has to
prevent from happening

00:09:22.667 --> 00:09:24.292
to one Reddit user who hopes

00:09:24.375 --> 00:09:27.000
Bob will come back from
the dead at some point,

00:09:27.083 --> 00:09:28.667
keeping the Bob dream alive.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:29.708
You've got to love it.

00:09:29.792 --> 00:09:32.083
I hope it doesn't suck.

00:09:32.167 --> 00:09:34.250
Of course, we won't know
if any of this is true

00:09:34.333 --> 00:09:36.333
until part one of
&lt;i&gt;Stranger Things &lt;/i&gt;season four

00:09:36.417 --> 00:09:38.542
arrives on May 27.

00:09:38.625 --> 00:09:40.500
And a huge part of
the fun is speculating

00:09:40.583 --> 00:09:43.042
and digging through old
episodes for inspiration.

00:09:43.125 --> 00:09:45.708
Why not share
your wildest theories

00:09:45.792 --> 00:09:46.667
in the comments below?

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.625
We promise not to rub them
in your face

00:09:48.708 --> 00:09:50.583
when part one lands in May.

00:09:50.667 --> 00:09:53.583
And make sure to subscribe
to Still Watching Netflix

00:09:53.667 --> 00:09:56.958
for more features about your
favourite films and shows.

